# WireMesh controller configuration (systemd EnvironmentFile).
# The controller is entirely env-configured. Defaults shown; uncomment to change.
# The controller's OWN state dir (CA key/cert + the SQLite DB), deliberately
# split from the gateway's /var/lib/wiremesh so the two can share a host: that
# directory belongs to the gateway (root-owned 0700, and the gateway unit drops
# CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE), so a controller running as `wiremesh` there either can't
# read it or steals it from the gateway. The unit's
# StateDirectory=wiremesh-controller creates this path owned wiremesh:wiremesh.
# Upgrading from a release that defaulted to /var/lib/wiremesh? The package
# postinstall migrates the controller's files here automatically; if you'd
# rather keep the old path, set it back explicitly below AND add it to
# ReadWritePaths= in a drop-in for wiremesh-controller.service.
WIREMESH_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/wiremesh-controller
# Bind enroll/sync/observe to all interfaces so remote gateways can reach them.
# (Admin TCP is ALWAYS loopback-only regardless of this.)
WIREMESH_BIND_IP=0.0.0.0
# WIREMESH_TCP_PORT=9400          # enrollment (server-TLS)
# WIREMESH_SYNC_TCP_PORT=9500     # Sync (mTLS)
# WIREMESH_OBSERVE_UDP_PORT=9600  # endpoint observation
# WIREMESH_ADMIN_TCP_PORT=9443    # admin (loopback-only)
